# Overlord Local Workflow

- If the session was launched by Overlord Desktop or CLI, attach first with `ovld protocol attach --mission-id $MISSION_ID`, update during work, ask when blocked, and deliver last.
- If the user asks from chat to use Overlord, use `/prompt` for new missions, `/load` for read-only context by mission ID, `/connect` to route the session onto an existing mission, and `/attach` when the user explicitly wants execution.
- If you need other protocol commands or flags, run `ovld protocol help` instead of guessing.

Normal delivery is summary-only; the objective ledger syncs independently. Use `ovld protocol changes` only to inspect ledger sync and hook health, never to infer ownership from a shared worktree.
**Never revert, restore, or delete file changes from other agents or missions.** Leave unrelated dirty files intact.
